== writing SPARQL queries ==


The listings package allows to highlight SPARQL Syntax. 


  ...
  \usepackage{listings}

  ...

  \lstset{language=SPARQL}
  \begin{lstlisting}
  PREFIX abc:<http://example.com/> 
  SELECT * FROM abc:test
  {
    {
     ?s <http://example.com/label> "test"^^abc:string .
    }
    UNION
    {
     ?s <http://example.com/label> "toast"^^abc:string .
     ?s ?p ?o .
     FILTER (?o != "toast")
    }
  }
  \end{lstlisting}
